Relevant columns and why they matter  
• races.year – season we are working in.  
• races.round – lets us spot the last GP of every season (MAX(round)).  
• races.race_id – technical key used to join every “_standings” or “results” table to the correct race.  

• constructor_standings.constructor_id – the team we are measuring.  
• constructor_standings.points – cumulative team points **after** each race; take the row from the last round to get the season‑total.  
• constructor_standings.race_id – join to races to pick the final race only.  

• driver_standings.driver_id – the driver whose points we need.  
• driver_standings.points – cumulative driver points; again use the final race for the season total.  
• driver_standings.race_id – join to races to restrict to the season‑ending race.  

• results.driver_id, results.constructor_id, results.race_id – tells us which constructor every driver was racing for in that Grand Prix; needed to link a driver‑standing row to the correct constructor.  

• constructors.constructor_id, constructors.name – readable team names in the final output.  

Typical conditions we will use  
• WHERE races.year = ?                           – filter to a single season (or none to do all).  
• AND races.round = (SELECT MAX(round) …)       – keep only the season’s final GP.  
• GROUP BY constructor_id                       – aggregate per constructor.  
• MAX(driver_standings.points)                  – pick the best driver of each constructor.  
• ORDER BY combined_points DESC LIMIT 3         – get the Top‑3 constructor / year combinations.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
10 exploratory / stepping‑stone queries
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Distinct seasons and how many GPs each contains
SELECT year, COUNT(*) AS grand_prix_cnt
FROM races
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Find the final round number (season‑ending GP) of every season
SELECT year, MAX(round) AS final_round
FROM races
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Constructor‑standings rows for the very first GP (race_id = 1) – quick data peek
SELECT DISTINCT constructor_id, points, position
FROM constructor_standings
WHERE race_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Constructor points at the final GP of the 2009 season
SELECT c.name, cs.points
FROM races            AS r
JOIN constructor_standings AS cs ON cs.race_id = r.race_id
JOIN constructors     AS c  ON c.constructor_id = cs.constructor_id
WHERE r.year = 2009
  AND r.round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2009)
ORDER BY cs.points DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Driver points at the 2009 season finale
SELECT d.forename || ' ' || d.surname AS driver_name,
       ds.points
FROM races              AS r
JOIN driver_standings   AS ds ON ds.race_id = r.race_id
JOIN drivers            AS d  ON d.driver_id = ds.driver_id
WHERE r.year = 2009
  AND r.round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2009)
ORDER BY ds.points DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Which constructor each driver represented in that same final GP (2009)
SELECT res.driver_id,
       res.constructor_id,
       c.name AS constructor_name
FROM results         AS res
JOIN races           AS r  ON r.race_id = res.race_id
JOIN constructors    AS c  ON c.constructor_id = res.constructor_id
WHERE r.year = 2009
  AND r.round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2009)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Best‑driver points per constructor in 2009 (season total)
SELECT t.constructor_id,
       MAX(t.points) AS best_driver_points
FROM (
    SELECT res.constructor_id, ds.points
    FROM races            AS r
    JOIN driver_standings AS ds  ON ds.race_id = r.race_id
    JOIN results          AS res ON res.race_id = ds.race_id
                                AND res.driver_id = ds.driver_id
    WHERE r.year = 2009
      AND r.round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2009)
) AS t
GROUP BY t.constructor_id
ORDER BY best_driver_points DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. 2009 – combined (team + best driver) points for every constructor
SELECT c.name,
       combo.constructor_points,
       combo.best_driver_points,
       combo.constructor_points + combo.best_driver_points AS combined_points
FROM (
    /* team points */
    SELECT cs.constructor_id,
           cs.points                              AS constructor_points,
           ( SELECT MAX(ds.points)
             FROM driver_standings ds
             JOIN results res ON res.race_id = cs.race_id
                              AND res.driver_id = ds.driver_id
                              AND res.constructor_id = cs.constructor_id
             WHERE ds.race_id = cs.race_id
           )                                      AS best_driver_points
    FROM races r
    JOIN constructor_standings cs ON cs.race_id = r.race_id
    WHERE r.year = 2009
      AND r.round = (SELECT MAX(round) FROM races WHERE year = 2009)
) AS combo
JOIN constructors c ON c.constructor_id = combo.constructor_id
ORDER BY combined_points DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Combined points for *all* seasons; show the 10 highest records
SELECT combo.year,
       c.name              AS constructor_name,
       combo.combined_points
FROM (
    SELECT r.year,
           cs.constructor_id,
           cs.points + MAX(ds.points) AS combined_points
    FROM races r
    JOIN constructor_standings cs ON cs.race_id = r.race_id
    JOIN driver_standings ds ON ds.race_id = cs.race_id
    JOIN results res ON res.race_id = ds.race_id
                     AND res.driver_id = ds.driver_id
                     AND res.constructor_id = cs.constructor_id
    JOIN (
        SELECT year, MAX(round) AS final_round
        FROM races
        GROUP BY year
    ) fin ON fin.year = r.year AND fin.final_round = r.round
    GROUP BY r.year, cs.constructor_id, cs.points
) AS combo
JOIN constructors c ON c.constructor_id = combo.constructor_id
ORDER BY combo.combined_points DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Pick the TOP‑3 (constructor, season) combinations with the largest combined points
SELECT *
FROM (
    SELECT combo.year,
           c.name AS constructor_name,
           combo.combined_points,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY combo.combined_points DESC) AS rn
    FROM (
        SELECT r.year,
               cs.constructor_id,
               cs.points + MAX(ds.points) AS combined_points
        FROM races r
        JOIN constructor_standings cs ON cs.race_id = r.race_id
        JOIN driver_standings ds ON ds.race_id = cs.race_id
        JOIN results res ON res.race_id = ds.race_id
                         AND res.driver_id = ds.driver_id
                         AND res.constructor_id = cs.constructor_id
        JOIN (
            SELECT year, MAX(round) AS final_round
            FROM races
            GROUP BY year
        ) fin ON fin.year = r.year AND fin.final_round = r.round
        GROUP BY r.year, cs.constructor_id, cs.points
    ) AS combo
    JOIN constructors c ON c.constructor_id = combo.constructor_id
) AS ranked
WHERE rn <= 3
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is intended for inspection, from simple listings (Query 1‑3) through progressively more sophisticated joins and aggregations, culminating in Query 10 which returns exactly the information asked for: the three highest combined (team + best‑driver) point totals and the seasons in which they occurred.
